entious, sometimes adopts wrong tone, can be uncooperative (Sarah mentioned). Candidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Also we have from structured notes: C is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere (from Sarah). Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as loner.\n\nWe need to decide our recommendation. We can either stay with Candidate C, or shift back to B, or consider others. Let's evaluate: B has strong reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, but uncooperative and pretentious. C has reliability, positive crew atmosphere, decision quality, attention, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is essential; uncooperative is a serious red flag. C's communication difficulty also a concern, but positive atmosphere suggests he works well with crew despite difficulty? Might be contradictory. But we have evidence that C puts concern for others above everything, which suggests good teamwork. Egocentric may conflict, but maybe less severe than uncooperative. Also C's adaptability is low (not willing to further education). For long-distance pilot, adaptability is important. B's adaptability unknown but likely better. D has responsibility, problem solving, but moody and loner. A has leadership but unfriendly and unhealthy.\n\nGiven the trade-offs, we might still lean towards Candidate C as best overall, but we could ask for more info on C's stress resilience or technical competence. However we need to make a contribution now. We could say we remain with Candidate C, but note concerns about C's communication and adaptability, and ask panel for any observations on C's stress handling or technical depth. Or we could shift to Candidate D? Probably not.\n\nThus as Emily Brooks, I will state my current recommendation: Candidate C, aligning with Sarah, but note concerns and request additional info on C's stress resilience and technical competence. Provide evidence: 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, decision quality, attention skills. Also note communication difficulty and egocentric as concerns. Conclude that C still seems best, but need more info on stress resilience.\n\nWe need to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
